WEBVTT

00:00:02.630 --> 00:00:07.610
You might not be able to 
keep running for much longer.

00:00:08.450 --> 00:00:10.820
You're right.

00:00:12.710 --> 00:00:17.770
<i>Somehow I thought I'd get
to decide when I went home.</i>

00:00:19.080 --> 00:00:20.040
<i>But...</i>

00:00:22.440 --> 00:00:23.980
<i>That's not how it is.</i>

00:00:24.680 --> 00:00:26.410
<i>That's not how it is at all!</i>

00:00:31.260 --> 00:00:34.300
<i>My brother's here. I have to go home.</i>

00:00:34.760 --> 00:00:36.590
<i>I have to go home now.</i>

00:00:52.210 --> 00:00:54.720
<b>I'll be done around 8 tonight. Need anything else? 

00:00:58.470 --> 00:00:59.820
Yoshida-san.

00:02:37.420 --> 00:02:42.050
"Summer Festival"

00:02:47.560 --> 00:02:49.580
Y-Yuzuha-san?

00:02:49.580 --> 00:02:52.350
Wow. Did I scare you that much?

00:02:53.220 --> 00:02:54.760
N-No.

00:02:56.120 --> 00:02:58.360
Sayu-chan, you're here to shop?

00:02:58.360 --> 00:03:02.460
Y-Yeah... I remembered
that the fridge is empty.

00:03:02.460 --> 00:03:04.680
It's really impressive 
how you do the chores every day.

00:03:04.680 --> 00:03:07.320
No, it's not really impressive.

00:03:09.220 --> 00:03:11.680
What are you doing here?

00:03:11.680 --> 00:03:13.580
I came to see a movie.

00:03:13.580 --> 00:03:15.900
I stop here a lot on my way
home from work.

00:03:15.900 --> 00:03:18.490
I see. So that's why.

00:03:21.780 --> 00:03:23.180
What's wrong, Sayu-chan?

00:03:23.660 --> 00:03:26.280
Somebody's looking for me.

00:03:26.280 --> 00:03:28.640
Over there, in front of you.

00:03:29.400 --> 00:03:30.850
You know them?

00:03:33.370 --> 00:03:36.860
Did they see you?

00:03:38.160 --> 00:03:39.320
No.

00:03:39.320 --> 00:03:41.780
They haven't started looking over here.

00:03:42.480 --> 00:03:44.970
Let's get out of here before they do.

00:03:45.730 --> 00:03:47.760
You can trust me.

00:03:47.760 --> 00:03:49.040
Okay.

00:03:49.040 --> 00:03:52.000
<b>Karaoke</b>

00:03:54.020 --> 00:03:56.090
I guess we're safe for now.

00:03:56.090 --> 00:03:58.960
Um, thank you.

00:03:58.960 --> 00:04:01.420
We all need to help each other out 
when we're in trouble, right?

00:04:04.660 --> 00:04:05.430
What's wrong?

00:04:06.420 --> 00:04:09.180
I was going to tell Yoshida-san.

00:04:09.520 --> 00:04:10.970
Do it.

00:04:11.620 --> 00:04:12.790
But...

00:04:13.390 --> 00:04:17.110
<b>Sorry, I'll be working late again, it looks like.</b>

00:04:14.290 --> 00:04:16.700
But I'm not sure what to say.

00:04:18.230 --> 00:04:20.310
Just say what's going on.

00:04:20.920 --> 00:04:25.240
"Somebody's chasing me. 
I ran into Mishima Yuzuha,

00:04:25.240 --> 00:04:28.820
and now we're hiding at the
karaoke place near the station."

00:04:31.470 --> 00:04:34.340
Oh, right. I get it.

00:04:38.060 --> 00:04:43.970
We need to tell him, or he'll start
searching the whole city for you.

00:04:44.280 --> 00:04:45.720
Does this work?

00:04:45.720 --> 00:04:48.680
<b>Sayu-chan and I are having a good time. 
If you want to join in, come to the karaoke place by the station.</b>

00:04:50.400 --> 00:04:52.930
Thank you, really.

00:04:54.850 --> 00:04:56.650
Now, since we're here...

00:04:59.950 --> 00:05:01.160
You done?

00:05:02.070 --> 00:05:04.240
You need to get home.

00:05:04.240 --> 00:05:06.510
Sayu-chan's waiting for you.

00:05:13.310 --> 00:05:14.080
What's wrong?

00:05:14.410 --> 00:05:19.050
"Having a good time"? I don't understand.

00:05:28.770 --> 00:05:32.720
Wow, my throat is hoarse.

00:05:32.720 --> 00:05:34.390
You don't want to sing?

00:05:34.390 --> 00:05:37.850
Not really. I don't know any songs.

00:05:38.550 --> 00:05:41.640
You've never done karaoke 
with your friends?

00:05:41.640 --> 00:05:42.570
Nope.

00:05:44.200 --> 00:05:48.280
Maybe kids these days don't do karaoke.

00:05:50.660 --> 00:05:51.770
Can I sit here?

00:05:51.770 --> 00:05:53.160
Okay.

00:05:59.120 --> 00:06:00.330
Now then...

00:06:00.870 --> 00:06:03.340
So somebody's chasing you, huh?

00:06:04.160 --> 00:06:05.880
I guess.

00:06:05.880 --> 00:06:07.550
I guess I should I ask...

00:06:08.080 --> 00:06:10.480
You're not running from some crime, right?

00:06:10.480 --> 00:06:12.180
Not at all!

00:06:14.280 --> 00:06:15.520
But...

00:06:18.050 --> 00:06:20.310
I won't ask for specifics.

00:06:20.310 --> 00:06:23.030
Yoshida-senpai told me most of it.

00:06:26.000 --> 00:06:27.950
Thank you.

00:06:28.440 --> 00:06:29.690
But you know...

00:06:30.180 --> 00:06:35.380
If they're here, that means 
you don't have a lot of time left.

00:06:36.470 --> 00:06:37.790
I know.

00:06:38.900 --> 00:06:40.250
You do, really?

00:06:40.600 --> 00:06:41.360
Yeah.

00:06:41.360 --> 00:06:46.090
But if you do, why are you out shopping?

00:06:46.090 --> 00:06:48.420
It doesn't seem that you really get it.

00:06:48.420 --> 00:06:53.110
Our deal is that I get to stay at Yoshida-san's
apartment because I do the chores.

00:06:53.650 --> 00:06:57.390
No matter what's going on, 
I need to keep it up.

00:06:57.390 --> 00:07:01.260
No, you've got bigger problems now, clearly.

00:07:03.420 --> 00:07:07.360
Yoshida-senpai's not going to drop dead 
because you didn't do the chores.

00:07:07.360 --> 00:07:09.820
And he's not going to kick you out.

00:07:09.820 --> 00:07:10.570
Well...

00:07:10.570 --> 00:07:13.530
And what are you going to do 
about your relationship with him?

00:07:13.530 --> 00:07:15.780
"R-Relationship"?

00:07:16.160 --> 00:07:18.110
Your relationship!

00:07:18.110 --> 00:07:22.840
You know the two of you are psychologically 
dependent on each other now.

00:07:22.840 --> 00:07:25.500
If you're suddenly torn apart, 
can you still get by?

00:07:30.050 --> 00:07:33.220
How do you feel about Yoshida-senpai?

00:07:33.940 --> 00:07:37.210
Is he just a guy that's helping you? 
Or are you in love?

00:07:37.210 --> 00:07:38.850
N-No, I...

00:07:38.850 --> 00:07:45.410
Either way, you had a goal when you ran away 
and ended up in Yoshida-senpai's house.

00:07:45.410 --> 00:07:47.610
Did you achieve it?

00:07:48.280 --> 00:07:50.860
If they take you away before you do,

00:07:50.860 --> 00:07:53.690
is that worth it? For your life,

00:07:53.690 --> 00:07:58.020
for the people who spent their time 
with you here?

00:08:05.530 --> 00:08:08.260
Sorry. You don't have to answer that.

00:08:08.850 --> 00:08:11.010
That was a mean thing to say.

00:08:11.010 --> 00:08:13.220
No, um...

00:08:15.000 --> 00:08:20.180
I think a girl your age 
may not be able to understand this.

00:08:20.650 --> 00:08:24.390
But there are some people you can only
meet now. And things you can only do now.

00:08:27.110 --> 00:08:31.320
You said you get that you
don't have much time, right?

00:08:31.740 --> 00:08:36.280
So you need to think seriously about 
what you want to do now.

00:08:44.660 --> 00:08:46.540
You got here earlier than I thought.

00:08:46.540 --> 00:08:48.680
Why karaoke?

00:08:48.680 --> 00:08:52.700
We ran into each other in front of the station 
and came here to have a chat.

00:08:52.700 --> 00:08:54.000
Right, Sayu-chan?

00:08:54.000 --> 00:08:55.180
Uh, yeah...

00:08:55.180 --> 00:08:56.480
I see.

00:08:56.480 --> 00:08:58.800
So, are you done having fun?

00:08:59.640 --> 00:09:01.070
Y-Yeah.

00:09:01.070 --> 00:09:01.770
I see.

00:09:04.180 --> 00:09:05.440
Let's go home, then.

00:09:10.980 --> 00:09:12.360
I'll carry that, too.

00:09:12.360 --> 00:09:14.890
No, I'm fine. It's not heavy.

00:09:14.890 --> 00:09:16.620
You bought more snacks, right?

00:09:17.480 --> 00:09:20.770
The ones you like. They were on sale.

00:09:20.770 --> 00:09:23.340
Thanks. I'll have them before we eat dinner.

00:09:23.340 --> 00:09:25.050
Don't eat too many, okay?

00:09:25.050 --> 00:09:26.270
Right, right.

00:09:26.270 --> 00:09:29.290
Oh, Mishima, you want to join us?

00:09:30.060 --> 00:09:32.710
I feel like singing some more, 
so I'll stay here.

00:09:33.330 --> 00:09:34.200
Yeah?

00:09:34.200 --> 00:09:35.320
Yup!

00:09:35.320 --> 00:09:38.430
Um, thank you.

00:09:38.430 --> 00:09:40.090
Not at all.

00:09:40.090 --> 00:09:41.140
Good luck.

00:09:46.920 --> 00:09:47.660
So—

00:09:47.660 --> 00:09:48.730
It's fine!

00:09:49.140 --> 00:09:51.110
No, it's not.

00:09:51.560 --> 00:09:53.300
That's your bad habit showing again.

00:09:53.860 --> 00:09:58.730
Remember what I said? You may think 
you're trying to help people, but you're not.

00:10:00.100 --> 00:10:01.060
Okay...

00:10:01.540 --> 00:10:03.330
I'll take you to a movie soon.

00:10:03.760 --> 00:10:05.540
That's better.

00:10:07.010 --> 00:10:09.260
Okay, see you tomorrow.

00:10:09.260 --> 00:10:11.160
Yeah, see you tomorrow!

00:10:21.640 --> 00:10:23.030
It's not fair.

00:10:23.030 --> 00:10:25.180
It's not fair!

00:10:25.560 --> 00:10:28.900
He never looks at me that way!

00:10:29.680 --> 00:10:33.380
I love him, too!

00:10:34.210 --> 00:10:37.140
I love him as much as anybody!

00:10:45.840 --> 00:10:50.010
Hey, is there anything 
you really want to do now?

00:10:50.010 --> 00:10:51.250
What's this about?

00:10:51.640 --> 00:10:53.210
Just think about it.

00:10:56.220 --> 00:10:57.440
Nothing, really.

00:10:57.440 --> 00:10:58.810
I see...

00:10:59.380 --> 00:11:04.220
<b>Summer Festival</b>

00:11:01.250 --> 00:11:04.220
Oh, right. The summer festival's tomorrow.

00:11:04.220 --> 00:11:06.550
The summer festival, huh?

00:11:07.180 --> 00:11:11.140
<b>Summer Festival</b>

00:11:07.180 --> 00:11:11.140
<b>29th (Sunday) 4:00 PM</b>

00:11:07.180 --> 00:11:11.140
<b>Kanotoushi Hikawa Shrine</b>

00:11:11.800 --> 00:11:12.850
You want to go?

00:11:13.860 --> 00:11:15.600
But...

00:11:15.600 --> 00:11:18.060
It's fine. We can if you want.

00:11:19.810 --> 00:11:25.420
Yeah, I'd like to go 
to the summer festival with you.

00:11:34.360 --> 00:11:35.630
It makes a nice sound.

00:11:40.040 --> 00:11:42.050
I'm glad we were able to rent it.

00:11:42.350 --> 00:11:43.190
Yeah!

00:11:45.080 --> 00:11:51.400
I've only ever been to a festival 
a few times when I was little.

00:11:53.450 --> 00:11:56.060
I didn't have any friends to go with,

00:11:56.060 --> 00:11:58.440
and I never really felt like going.

00:11:58.970 --> 00:12:00.330
I see...

00:12:01.400 --> 00:12:05.870
But I decided I'd like to go with you.

00:12:08.390 --> 00:12:10.100
I guess it's already started.

00:12:14.540 --> 00:12:16.380
It really is a festival.

00:12:16.380 --> 00:12:19.060
"Really is"? You're silly.

00:12:20.440 --> 00:12:21.510
Hey, Yoshida-san.

00:12:21.990 --> 00:12:24.560
Why won't you look at me?

00:12:24.560 --> 00:12:26.250
Oh, that?

00:12:26.870 --> 00:12:27.970
Yoshida-san?

00:12:35.910 --> 00:12:37.860
Do you like my yukata?

00:12:42.710 --> 00:12:43.610
It's pretty.

00:12:51.930 --> 00:12:56.570
Prettier than Gotou-san?

00:12:57.140 --> 00:13:00.040
No, it's nothing! Never mind.

00:13:00.040 --> 00:13:03.030
What? Now I'm really curious.

00:13:03.940 --> 00:13:05.360
Jealous, huh?

00:13:05.360 --> 00:13:09.280
Gimme some, Bro! Gimme some!

00:13:09.280 --> 00:13:11.080
Cotton candy, huh?

00:13:11.080 --> 00:13:12.340
Want some?

00:13:13.010 --> 00:13:16.080
Yeah. I always have.

00:13:16.080 --> 00:13:19.860
When I went as a kid, 
they wouldn't get me any.

00:13:20.190 --> 00:13:23.600
I really remember that time.

00:13:23.600 --> 00:13:25.420
Let's go get some, then.

00:13:25.420 --> 00:13:26.570
Okay!

00:13:38.290 --> 00:13:40.200
So this is how they make it?

00:13:40.200 --> 00:13:41.600
Here you go.

00:13:41.600 --> 00:13:42.810
Thanks.

00:13:43.910 --> 00:13:45.150
I'll pay.

00:13:45.150 --> 00:13:47.180
No, I can pay for it.

00:13:47.550 --> 00:13:51.110
That's not the issue. 
It's not expensive. I can—

00:13:55.040 --> 00:13:58.560
No... Yeah. I get it now.

00:13:59.350 --> 00:14:02.270
It's fine. I'd like to buy it for you.

00:14:04.210 --> 00:14:05.110
Okay.

00:14:15.430 --> 00:14:18.370
Wow! It melts in an instant!

00:14:18.700 --> 00:14:20.380
It's just sugar.

00:14:20.830 --> 00:14:24.860
Don't laugh. It's my first time trying it.

00:14:24.860 --> 00:14:27.470
Oh, right. Sorry.

00:14:27.470 --> 00:14:29.030
As long as you understand.

00:14:31.540 --> 00:14:36.270
The way cotton candy is kind of sticky, 
and the way it melts instantly in your mouth...

00:14:36.980 --> 00:14:40.780
If I hadn't met you, I never would've known.

00:14:40.780 --> 00:14:42.520
That's not true.

00:14:42.520 --> 00:14:44.680
So here's my way of saying, "Thanks."

00:14:46.110 --> 00:14:47.690
Here you go! Say, "Ah!"

00:14:51.040 --> 00:14:53.480
Hurry up, or it'll melt.

00:15:01.440 --> 00:15:03.180
It's really sweet.

00:15:03.180 --> 00:15:05.000
Y-Yeah.

00:15:05.510 --> 00:15:07.010
Thanks!

00:15:10.240 --> 00:15:11.740
O-Ow...

00:15:11.740 --> 00:15:13.610
Sorry, miss.

00:15:13.610 --> 00:15:15.850
It's fine. Be careful, okay?

00:15:15.850 --> 00:15:16.780
Okay.

00:15:18.150 --> 00:15:20.710
Yoshida-san... Thank you.

00:15:23.140 --> 00:15:26.230
We won't get lost like this,
either, so it's even better!

00:15:35.670 --> 00:15:37.460
Fireworks!

00:15:40.370 --> 00:15:42.380
It's so pretty!

00:15:42.380 --> 00:15:45.620
I've never seen fireworks so close.

00:15:45.620 --> 00:15:47.850
Yeah, really.

00:15:47.850 --> 00:15:50.950
I didn't realize there was a festival 
like this so close to home.

00:15:53.910 --> 00:15:58.280
<i>Without Sayu, I'd never have come here.</i>

00:16:02.080 --> 00:16:03.520
What's wrong, Yoshida-san?

00:16:04.130 --> 00:16:06.270
No, it's nothing.

00:16:06.680 --> 00:16:09.220
What? I'm curious.

00:16:09.810 --> 00:16:13.400
Look, the next one's 
probably gonna be really big.

00:16:13.400 --> 00:16:14.180
Yeah.

00:16:24.500 --> 00:16:29.690
<i>If it weren't for Sayu... 
If I hadn't met Sayu...</i>

00:16:51.570 --> 00:16:52.960
Sayu!

00:16:52.960 --> 00:16:53.960
Sayu!

00:16:53.960 --> 00:16:54.950
Yoshida-san?

00:16:57.400 --> 00:16:58.240
What's wrong?

00:16:58.650 --> 00:17:01.720
I told you I was going 
to throw out the trash, right?

00:17:04.610 --> 00:17:08.620
Oh, right. Trash. That's right.

00:17:24.980 --> 00:17:26.620
Hey, Yoshida-san...

00:17:27.060 --> 00:17:30.010
Did you think I'd disappeared?

00:17:30.010 --> 00:17:32.090
Y-Yeah, I guess.

00:17:33.570 --> 00:17:37.420
You'd really freak out if I disappeared, huh?

00:17:41.800 --> 00:17:43.190
Yeah.

00:17:48.450 --> 00:17:52.920
For a minute, I thought you'd disappeared. 
And I got really worried.

00:17:55.890 --> 00:17:59.240
I-I see. Sorry.

00:17:59.240 --> 00:18:00.970
Why are you apologizing?

00:18:07.970 --> 00:18:08.730
Hey...

00:18:10.880 --> 00:18:13.650
Are you really going home?

00:18:15.490 --> 00:18:18.050
No, forget it!

00:18:18.050 --> 00:18:19.160
O-Okay.

00:18:38.320 --> 00:18:39.860
It's over, huh?

00:18:39.860 --> 00:18:41.420
Yeah, it is.

00:18:42.370 --> 00:18:44.360
Let's get going.

00:18:45.620 --> 00:18:46.700
What's wrong, Sayu?

00:18:47.140 --> 00:18:53.690
I gave a different name 
to all the guys, except you.

00:18:55.430 --> 00:19:00.740
I gave them a fake name each time 
I moved to a new place to stay.

00:19:03.200 --> 00:19:04.540
But...

00:19:04.540 --> 00:19:07.540
When you asked for my name,

00:19:08.100 --> 00:19:10.180
it really surprised me, but...

00:19:10.760 --> 00:19:13.220
My real name slipped out of my mouth.

00:19:13.750 --> 00:19:15.000
I wonder why.

00:19:16.920 --> 00:19:22.560
After giving you my real name, 
I thought I might not be able to run anymore.

00:19:22.560 --> 00:19:26.280
At first, I was really negative about it.

00:19:26.280 --> 00:19:28.230
I see.

00:19:31.140 --> 00:19:33.160
Why did you ask me that?

00:19:34.880 --> 00:19:37.900
Do you not want me to go home?

00:19:52.800 --> 00:19:53.900
I...

00:19:56.930 --> 00:19:58.300
I...

00:20:04.770 --> 00:20:06.890
I think you should go home.

00:20:10.740 --> 00:20:12.600
Yeah, you're right.

00:20:15.480 --> 00:20:19.660
Thanks to you, 
I won't need to run away anymore.

00:20:19.660 --> 00:20:20.570
Yeah?

00:20:20.880 --> 00:20:24.680
Yoshida-san, if I weren't a teenage girl,

00:20:25.080 --> 00:20:27.720
and you saw me under that lamppost,

00:20:27.720 --> 00:20:29.540
would you still have taken me in?

00:20:29.920 --> 00:20:31.940
I think you would've.

00:20:32.370 --> 00:20:36.500
If I were an adult, would we have had sex?

00:20:38.360 --> 00:20:40.940
I'm sure we wouldn't have.

00:20:43.880 --> 00:20:45.580
And in the same way,

00:20:45.580 --> 00:20:49.380
even if you weren't a
salaryman with a beard...

00:20:50.680 --> 00:20:52.970
No, never mind.

00:20:52.970 --> 00:20:55.040
Let's go, Yoshida-san.

00:20:56.340 --> 00:20:58.610
What kind of miso soup 
should I make tomorrow?

00:20:59.190 --> 00:21:00.490
What would you like?

00:21:00.490 --> 00:21:03.530
Well, green onion.

00:21:03.530 --> 00:21:04.740
Okay, green onion!

00:21:18.390 --> 00:21:20.590
Who the hell is it?

00:21:22.680 --> 00:21:24.380
Should I answer it?

00:21:24.380 --> 00:21:27.820
No. It's probably just a package.

00:21:30.600 --> 00:21:32.070
Coming!

00:21:37.960 --> 00:21:40.010
Is this Yoshida-san's residence?

00:21:40.010 --> 00:21:41.070
Yes?

00:21:41.940 --> 00:21:45.320
My name is Ogiwara Issa.

00:21:45.320 --> 00:21:46.780
Ogiwara?

00:21:50.160 --> 00:21:52.660
Ogiwara Sayu's brother.

00:21:56.280 --> 00:21:59.350
I've come to bring Sayu home.

00:23:29.970 --> 00:23:34.970
<b>Next Time</b>

00:23:29.970 --> 00:23:34.970
"Past"

00:23:35.260 --> 00:23:39.980
<b>See You Next Week</b>
